{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Therefore say to the children of Israel: I am YHWH.</b> After he mentioned above, 'And Elohim spoke further to Moshe, So shall you say to the children of Israel: YHWH, the God of your fathers,' etc., and commanded him to make known to Israel the special Name, he returned and commanded him again here to make it known to them a second time, and commanded him to assure them with the four expressions of redemption: והוצאתי, והצלתי, וגאלתי, ולקחתי. And he announced to them in them four tidings: the first, that they would be released from the bondage while still under their jurisdiction; the second, that they would be released from them completely from under their jurisdiction; the third, that he assured them of the splitting of the Sea of Reeds; the fourth, that he assured them of the giving of the Torah. That they would be released from the bondage — this is what he said: <b>And I will bring you out from under the burdens of Egypt.</b> And this is the assurance that they would be released from the bondage while still under their jurisdiction; and so we find that this was so for six months, as the Sages, may their memory be blessed, said: on Rosh HaShanah the labor ceased for our forefathers in Egypt, and the redemption was imminent on the fifteenth of Nisan. That they would be released from under their jurisdiction completely — this is what he said: <b>And I will deliver you from their service.</b> And this is the assurance that they would go out from under their jurisdiction and no longer be under their rule for any labor-tax at all, but would be complete free men. The matter of the splitting of the Sea of Reeds — this is what he said: <b>And I will redeem you with an outstretched arm and with great judgments.</b> And this is an allusion to the splitting of the Sea of Reeds, for then they were considered redeemed, since a slave who goes out from under the hand of a harsh master who embittered his life with many kinds of labors and was forced to send him away and make him a free man against his will — the slave still fears and trembles lest his master pursue him, and the redemption is not complete for the slave until it is confirmed by the death of the master. And this is why the expression of redemption is not found in the Exodus from Egypt except after the destruction of the Egyptians, as it is said (Exodus 14:27): ״וינער ה׳ את מצרים בתוך הים״, and adjacent to it: ״ויושע ה׳ ביום ההוא את ישראל״ — for then they were considered redeemed and saved, and then the salvation was complete. And what he mentioned, 'with an outstretched arm,' is because it is written regarding the splitting of the Sea of Reeds (ibid.): ״וירא ישראל את היד הגדולה״, and concerning this the prophet mentioned (Isaiah 51:9): ״עורי עורי לבשי עוז זרוע ה׳״. And he mentioned 'with great judgments' because they were judged in the sea with many modes of judgment, as the Sages, may their memory be blessed, expounded: 'a horse and its rider He cast into the sea' — the horse was bound to the rider and the rider to the horse, and both would rise to the heights and descend to the depths, and they were not separated one from the other, in the manner of what is written (Exodus 15:5): ״ירדו במצולות כמו אבן יאכלמו כקש צללו כעופרת״." "The matter of the giving of the Torah — this is what is written (verse 7): <b>And I will take you to Me for a people,</b> and this is the assurance regarding the giving of the Torah, concerning which it is written (Deuteronomy 27:9): ״היום הזה נהיית לעם״. <b>And I will be to you for an Elohim</b> — you shall accept My divinity. <b>And you shall know</b> from then onward, <b>that I am YHWH your Elohim,</b> that I am the One performing for you signs and wonders, renewed in creation, because I am your Elohim, <b>who brings you out from under the burdens of Egypt,</b> that is to say, I am He who brings you out, for according to the arrangement of the stars they were still worthy of remaining there."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:56:32.061800504Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}